From 52c304bcdb178d335d5fbe8b10540a7ca42e5abc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: FCA11-long passive release frame + panda
 actuation-budget mirror (G7, fixes N1)

The panda's FCA11-long tx hook (safety/modes/hyundai.h:146-149, 939-975) caps a continuous
actuation episode at 2.5 s, then refuses actuation for a 3 s cooldown. An episode ends ONLY
on an ACCEPTED PASSIVE 0x38D frame from the host (L970-973) or by budget expiry (L948-951).
The car layer sent NOTHING when not braking (fca11_long.py:321-327 pre-G7): the camera's own
frame goes through the forward hook, not the transmit hook, so act_active stayed latched across
separate brakes and the budget kept running. Measured over route 149 (round-5, v8): only
45-57 % of the intended FCA11 brake time would actually actuate; ~10 requests per drive never
actuated at all. With a one-frame passive release that becomes 79-85 %.

- Passive release: on the braking true -> false edge, emit exactly ONE passive mirror frame -
  the camera's own idle shape (all brake fields 0, Warn 0, CmdAct 0, DecCmdAct 0), fresh alive
  + CRC, every other byte the camera's. The panda accepts it while controls_allowed AND
  heartbeat_engaged; it is the clean release / hand-back frame that ENDS the episode and
  starts the cooldown clock. Only sent when a fresh camera frame is in hand (never hardcoded),
  on the same 50 Hz slot as the actuating frames.
- Budget mirror: the 2.5 s / 3 s budget is mirrored in Python (FCA11_BUDGET_FRAMES /
  FCA11_COOLDOWN_FRAMES, from the same hyundai.h constants). The car layer now deliberately
  ENDS the episode at the budget edge (with its passive frame) and does not re-command inside
  the cooldown, so `braking` - and therefore the gas hard-zero and the alerts - matches what
  the panda will really accept, instead of issuing frames the panda silently refuses.
- Tests: car-layer tests assert exactly one passive frame closes every episode (and the OFF
  path emits none) and that the budget mirror stops/restarts the episode on the panda's clock;
  two panda tests pin the defect (two brakes with no passive frame between them are ONE episode,
  the second cut at the 2.5 s edge) and prove the passive frame re-arms the budget.

No panda firmware change: the passive frame and the budget constants already exist in
safety/modes/hyundai.h (148-149, 903-931, 943-976) and are already covered by its own tests;
this is a Python-only change. The panda TX hook and the budget/cooldown behaviour are untouched.
